// v2288 -- box3d artifact self-heal, shared by POST /box3d/pull-from-peer AND the peer-discovery auto-step.
// The WASM is portable (a module built on the Mac runs bit-identically in any box's browser), so a box that
// cannot build locally copies a peer's built box3d.{js,wasm} into its own vendor/box3d. Factored into ONE
// function so the manual endpoint and the automatic heal run the exact same code. As a bonus, when every box
// pulls the SAME binary from one builder, cross-machine determinism (the lockstep precondition) is trivially
// satisfied -- it is literally the same wasm, not two independent compiler outputs.
// v2517 -- WHAT BUILD IS THIS? "Ready" used to mean "both files exist", which is why a box could sit on a stale
// box3d.wasm forever: it existed, so nothing ever offered it a newer one. Keith hit exactly that -- Galaxina had a
// pre-v2508 binary, was "ready", and only got a new one because he clicked Build/Pull by hand.
//
